From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 12:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: clamp rate-control bandwidth

When an AP runs a wider channel than a station currently uses, mt7996 can
pass the BSS bandwidth to firmware rate control through ra->bw. That may let
firmware select rates wider than the peer's current operating bandwidth.

Clamp the RA bandwidth to the smaller of the BSS channel width and the
station's current operating bandwidth. Keep the PHY bandwidth in sync and
leave the operating-mode fields at their default values; forcing those
VHT-shaped fields for ordinary HE stations can confuse MT7996 firmware rate
selection.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -2753,6 +2753,7 @@
 	struct mt76_phy *mphy = mt76_vif_link_phy(&link->mt76);
 	struct cfg80211_bitrate_mask *mask = &link->bitrate_mask;
 	u32 cap = link_sta->sta->wme ? STA_CAP_WMM : 0;
+	u8 chan_bw, op_bw;
 	struct cfg80211_chan_def *chandef;
 	struct sta_rec_ra_uni *ra;
 	enum nl80211_band band;
@@ -2773,8 +2774,10 @@
 	ra->auto_rate = true;
 	ra->phy_mode = mt76_connac_get_phy_mode(mphy, vif, band, link_sta);
 	ra->channel = chandef->chan->hw_value;
-	ra->bw = (link_sta->bandwidth == IEEE80211_STA_RX_BW_320) ?
-		 CMD_CBW_320MHZ : link_sta->bandwidth;
+	chan_bw = mt76_connac_chan_bw(chandef);
+	op_bw = link_sta->bandwidth == IEEE80211_STA_RX_BW_320 ?
+		CMD_CBW_320MHZ : link_sta->bandwidth;
+	ra->bw = min_t(u8, chan_bw, op_bw);
 	ra->phy.bw = ra->bw;
 	ra->mmps_mode = mt7996_mcu_get_mmps_mode(link_sta->smps_mode);
 
